      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-56" id="fn-56" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:12pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%;text-decoration:underline">Adjustment for ACA Purposes:</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The volumes in column (c) include volumes received from storage and transported under Northwest&#8217;s TF-2 Firm Redelivery Transportation service and other firm and interruptible transportation services to redeliver gas stored in (1) the Jackson Prairie Storage Project under Rate Schedules SGS-2F, SGS-2I or PAL, and (2) the Plymouth LNG Facility under Rate Schedules LS-2F or LS-2I. Northwest assesses the ACA surcharge on all transportation volumes that are delivered into the Jackson Prairie Storage Project and the Plymouth LNG Facility. Consequently, the ACA surcharge should not be assessed on volumes a second time when they move out of storage. The (1) TF-2 Redelivery Transportation volumes reported on Page 305, Line 4, Column (j) and (2) other 2025 firm and interruptible transportation volumes of 44,523,393 Dth redelivered from the Jackson Prairie Storage Project and the Plymouth LNG Facility should be excluded for ACA billing purposes from the volumes reported on Page 520, Line No. 5, Column (c). The ACA volume that should be used for ACA billing purposes is 935,870,691 Dth (i.e., 935,870,691 Dth (Total Dekatherms, page 305 column j) - 6,684,991 Dth (TF-2, page 305 column j, line 4) - 37,838,402 Dth (TF-1 Storage Re-deliveries transported from storage).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-57" id="fn-57" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas of Others Received for Transmission represents scheduled receipt nominations net of in-kind fuel. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled receipt nominations and actual physical receipts are captured in the 806 imbalances and are included in the numbers shown on lines 10 and 25 of page 520. The in-kind reimbursements are shown on lines 13 and 14.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
